 = exit-quarter annualised (not summed)","prior":"","rows":[{"cur":655,"metric":"Revenue (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":null,"yoy":null},{"cur":28,"metric":"Operating Profit (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":null,"yoy":null},{"cur":4.3,"metric":"OPM (%)","nd":1,"pct":true,"prior":null,"yoy":null},{"cur":9,"metric":"PAT (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":null,"yoy":null},{"cur":0.54,"metric":"EPS (Rs, annualised, exit qtr)","nd":2,"pct":false,"prior":null,"yoy":null}]}},"profile":{"entities":"Wonder Electricals Ltd; none","mgmt":"","subseg":"BLDC fans; TPW fans; ventilating fans; electric heaters; electric kettles","themes":"BLDC adoption; seasonality mitigation; MSME payment compliance; capacity expansion"},"qtr":"Q2FY25","ratios":[{"label":"ROE %","value":"9.7%"},{"label":"ROCE %","value":"9.6%"},{"label":"D/E","value":"1.1x"},{"label":"Int cover","value":"2.4x"},{"label":"Receivable d","value":"139.0"},{"label":"Inventory d","value":"41.8"},{"label":"Payable d","value":"115.2"},{"label":"OPM %","value":"4.3%"}],"s":"WEL","sec":"Home Appliances - Fan OEM/ODM","sec2":"Consumer Durables","sections":{"bull_bear":[{"body":"Primarily internal accruals for capex and working capital; modest bank term loans used; no dividends or buybacks mentioned; focus on reinvestment for capacity and product diversification.","src":"concall","title":"Capital allocation"},{"body":"High seasonality of fan demand; reliance on B2B customer relationships (no direct branding); potential margin pressure if BLDC growth slows; MSME payment compliance pressures on working capital; new product lines (heaters/kettles) unproven at scale.","src":"concall","title":"Risks & watch-items"},{"body":"Confident, experienced, and pragmatic; emphasis on delivery reliability, quality, and operational efficiency; avoids overpromising on new products; highlights long-term vendor relationships and lack of listed competition as key advantages.","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"The company's 'stickiness' with customers is unusually high — nearly all customers have stayed for decades, with attrition only when customers started their own units; this suggests deep operational trust, not just price-based loyalty.","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"}],"business":[{"body":"BLDC fans: 2.35 lakh units in H1FY25 (up from 60k in H1FY24, +291.6%); total units sold: 32.95 lakh in H1FY25; heaters/kettles: new product line, first-year, no revenue share disclosed; TPW fans: growing segment; ventilating fans: core offering.","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"> Only challenges the company specifically discussed on this call. Names resolved against our own companies/products files + StockMetadata. ✅=covered here, ⭐=sector-knowledge.\n\n> The two challenges discussed — fan-business seasonality (idle off-season capacity, mitigated by adding heaters/kettles) and the MSME payment-terms legislation requiring faster vendor payouts (handled via bill discounting, lifting working capital) — are internal/operational. Management names no specific suppliers, customers (confidentiality agreements), or repriced raw materials, and explicitly states there are no listed competitors in the OEM/ODM fan space. No tradeable third-party listed beneficiaries or losers are implicated.\n\n| Challenge (their words) | Beneficiary — NSE · BSE · Sector | Loser | Why / conviction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| — | — | — | — |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers (listed names)"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"EBITDA margin improved to 2.68% in H1FY25; BLDC fans have slightly better margins than induction fans; overall margin improvement driven by volume leverage, cost optimization, and product mix shift, not solely BLDC.","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"H1 FY25 revenue was INR361cr (+101% YoY); company aims to maintain similar growth for full FY25; no formal full-year guidance given but management expressed confidence in sustaining momentum.","src":"concall","title":"Guidance"},{"body":"Fully booked during peak season; idle capacity exists in off-season, partially offset by heaters/kettles production.","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"Expansion into TPW (table, pedestal, wall) plastic fan manufacturing via new INR3cr plant (to commission early FY26); potential to scale heaters/kettles into a material segment over 2-3 years; possible export entry in future.","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["Q2FY25 concall summary","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"Wonder Electricals is scaling as India's leading listed fan OEM/ODM, leveraging BLDC growth and off-season appliance diversification to drive 100%+ revenue growth and margin expansion, while strategically expanding capacity via internal accruals. The company's operational discipline, vendor stickiness, and lack of listed peers create a durable competitive moat.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":1.07,"fy":"FY26","mcap":1854,"opm":4.3,"pe":203.7,"roe":9.7}],"wtt":null},"drhp":{"rpt":{"financials":{"_source":"ledger","balance_sheet_key":[{"basis":"Standalone","cwip_amount_rs":0,"equity_share_capital_amount_rs":134000000,"fy":"FY2022","inventory_amount_rs":322100000,"net_fixed_assets_amount_rs":336900000,"networth_amount_rs":535400000,"other_equity_amount_rs":401400000,"total_assets_amount_rs":2248900000,"trade_payables_amount_rs":1435400000,"trade_receivables_amount_rs":1516600000},{"basis":"Standalone","equity_share_capital_amount_rs":134000000,"fy":"FY2023","inventory_amount_rs":370800000,"net_fixed_assets_amount_rs":328600000,"networth_amount_rs":596200000,"other_equity_amount_rs":462100000,"total_assets_amount_rs":2328700000,"trade_payables_amount_rs":1412600000,"trade_receivables_amount_rs":1564200000},{"basis":"Standalone","equity_share_capi